Go toolchain and container base image

The binary is compiled with the Go toolchain (golang image, pinned by digest, used only to build);
the Go standard library linked into it is BSD-3-Clause (https://go.dev/LICENSE). The image runs
FROM gcr.io/distroless/static:nonroot, pinned by digest (https://github.com/GoogleContainerTools/
distroless, Apache-2.0), which holds Debian's ca-certificates, tzdata, base-files and
netbase; their licenses are recorded in the image at /usr/share/doc/*/copyright. The image is not
part of this repository's source.

Vendored in this repository

internal/controller/assets/pixie/   Pixie's rendered Kubernetes manifests, Apache-2.0, with Pixie's
                                    LICENSE kept beside them (https://github.com/pixie-io/pixie)
hack/pixie-patches/                 patches to Pixie, under Pixie's Apache-2.0
Both leave the operator when Pixie is removed from the stack.

Installed at runtime, not distributed

The operator does not contain the software below. It installs it on a cluster, as upstream Helm
charts or upstream container images pulled by the cluster from their own registries, from
helmfile.yaml, the platform ClusterHelmRelease resources and the controllers' default images.
Each is under its own license, which applies to whoever runs it. Listed so an operator of a
cluster knows what it runs.

